statement_changes.new_statement:
\begin{proposition}[Sylvester, 1867]\label{conjectures:prop:kron}
If $H$ and $K$ are Hadamard matrices of positive orders $m$ and $n$, then
$H\otimes K$ is a Hadamard matrix of order $mn$. Define $S_1=(1)$ and,
for every integer $k\ge0$, set
\[
S_{2^{k+1}}=\begin{pmatrix}S_{2^k}&S_{2^k}\\S_{2^k}&-S_{2^k}\end{pmatrix}
=\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\1&-1\end{pmatrix}\otimes S_{2^k}.
\]
Then $S_{2^k}$ is Hadamard of order $2^k$ for every integer $k\ge0$.
\end{proposition}
